## Background

* The bills for this account were always high. Seemingly to a ridiculous amount when it came to gas.

* The combination of this factor and erratic approach to billing of the gas account in particular contributed significantly to a feeling that just as the account seemed to be under control, another very large bill threw it off balance again.

* The direct debit had rised at Octoput continuing insistence from an initial ~ £108 a month to £300. This happenedd in the first 2 XXX years of Octopus taking over the account.

* Despite payments of £3,600 a year and periods of the account balance heading towards ‘coming under control’ - at least once a year, and sometime more, very large bills  lead to the account lurching back into a seeming never ending debt position.

* In the summer of 2025 my son had the bright idea to photograph the meter and send the  photograph to Ocotpus (ref ##meter-photo).   

??? use or not or restaye without the son bit - I was going to mention it was never clear to me what figures were before and after the decimal point, but ...???

* It turned out that the estimated reading was far higher than the actual gas meter reading. This triggered my request for a refund.

* I had previously been concerned that the high readings for the gas coincided with the unusually high spike of gas prices in 2022/2023. 

* I therefore contacted Octopus to ascertain exactly how any refund would be calculated. In my mind at least, a significant amount had been incurred at the time of effective unit rates above 10p/kWh (the actual rates were up to 16p/kWh reduced bu Govt subsidy). NB: I never received any explanation.


## Complaint Details
   
### The refund calculation mechanism 

    • Despite formally asking at least two times in email {ref ##no-refund-calclulation##) no  explation was given to me.

    • When the refund arrived (ref ##refund-bill##) I was extrememly confused as to how the calculation had actually been made. 

    • I had expected something understandable in the form of: estimated value - actual value - for the kWh over-reach, backed up by a semi-algorithmic description of how the units had been valued and how the related to the price charged.

    • What turned up was the bill show in ref ##refund-bill##. There was insufficient detail in this bill - and they way it was presented - to clarify how the refund value had been arrived at. 

    • In particular it was not possible - given the way the bill had been structured - to work out what unit price had been assigned to the kWh units due for refund …  XXXMCC double check this.

Briefly (here) the bill indicated that XXMCC-DESCRIBE-FIRST-EXPERIENCEXX not full picture.

    • By this point I was completely confused -  but also extremely busy at work. I did expect to hear from Octopus in the then not to distant future. I heard nothing - apparently from  Octopus POV a cryptic bill

