### Pattern of over estimation

    • It is completely unclear why Octopus chose to use unreasonably large annual estimates for fuel consumption. 

    * However what is very clear is that their choice to seemingly arbitrarily do that has caused many issues.
    
    • For unknown reasons, Octopus’ annual gas usage estimate  (higher than 26,000 kWh) - is over double the Ofcom estimated assumption for a small (two bedrooms and a box room - technically three bedrooms) terraced house in west London occupied by three persons.

    • annual estimate values assigned to the account by Octopus:

    • It is only at the end of December 2025 that the estimate  is reduced to something akin to the OfCom ‘norm’.

